            "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqxLhiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQ+EQAAUdYC0a4tz5GkCzL3mtNnEL\nTF2tLRv9Y2RMvY6ZvrRY3tq+jvnu/mHwnIJFKWaubpBfSqkIsW3ymvxcYKXN6PRH\nRmhkwE3/cbtGKIzG018WpOJII4WLA397LYR4jqOxGBbOJBnU94Tk+ac6hhawuRiI\nRErNKk2pA9uALM2gaezsyTTTMOlHrGCl6XsR/gnN34ZxprKnMNVdvsIEJSTknBgJ\nac/HcPhT3kh4b80pno902ThlsHzUhARsSksJ+HsSk1pb2zdaluZaLbBpMybO8QN6\nucyWnXbJeeL1cKstfeCmDxM2DLTJErWP9atW51BbpiLc1aHEKa02+8Gf2VpFNd5V\nUm6TlqqqZPGMD0JGnufiRDz2m+45BeZBgdZZLJ0e9ICU30MDec8nlUQaJfdLtgze\nfo+nepKe7Qtav5NrPgbZOeTzIn++aRPvasMPQIfTF3wlqykw2Kph9e4KACzaBAIm\ntUywA2RIDzkW+Nlq8p+LiiiHMYtJa82+rzS/uWyu7GIdcjUA3chFVz8leSSUOvhm\nzoM7f1ET9OqfcjlYyNM2LBe+YPK2fCMz9vwhO/FJ1H3QNvzeXC7hNsE4teyrqEoA\nlUZTymlVem+n1MM7fMb2oQI/Za05z5LWBvbkEnO2743lOED41OacjPVDoAu58Cgf\nJ2wuWbGouz2jbjqriXlv\n=tOZq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n",
            "payload": "tree aa5ae06f2f3fd1ce7ee0671db56e1ed4a467bb88\nparent 7e053d76d0a2481b71db4cab5e84574ef754ac46\nauthor Andre Haikal <andrehaykal@gmail.com> 1791277138 +0000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791277138 +0000\n\nfeat(integrations): add support for Pleo MCP (#7767)\n\n## Problem\n\nConnecting Pleo's MCP server (`https://mcp.pleo.io/mcp`) through\n`mcp-generic` returns no refresh token, so connections expire after\nPleo's 7-day access-token lifetime. Each connect also registers a new\nclient named \"Nango Dynamic MCP Client\", which is what end users see on\nPleo's consent screen.\n\n## Solution\n\nAdd a dedicated `pleo-mcp` provider (`MCP_OAUTH2`, `client_registration:\ndynamic`), following `airtable-mcp`. Nango registers the client with\nPleo's `/oauth/register` endpoint automatically, asking for both\n`authorization_code` and `refresh_token`.\n\n- Authorization, token and registration endpoints on\n`https://mcp.pleo.io/oauth/`\n- `resource=https://mcp.pleo.io/`, default scope `authenticated`\n- Proxy base URL `https://mcp.pleo.io` with `accept:\napplication/json,text/event-stream`\n\nAlso adds the docs page, the logo (symlinked to `pleo.svg`), the\ndocs.json entry and regenerated LLM indexes.\n\nFollows up on a conversation with the Nango team, who recommended a\nseparate Pleo MCP provider over `mcp-generic`.\n\n## Testing\n\nProvider passes `scripts/validation/providers` schema validation.\nOutside Nango, a public client registered with Pleo using the same\nregistration metadata receives a refresh token, and refreshing it works.\nThe end-to-end Nango flow with this provider is not yet verified.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Andre Haikal <andre@askdragonfly.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
